# XSH cimag(), cimagf() and cimagl()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Only what the page makes exact is tested: values returned unchanged or with
# a stated sign change, including signed zeros, infinities and NaN parts.
# Arguments are built with CMPLX() and pass through volatile objects, and the
# three types (name, name with f, name with l) are each tested. Infinite and
# NaN cases are skipped where the type has none.

assertion  XSH.cimag.001
anchor     functions/cimag.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/cimag.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       cimag returns the imaginary part of a finite value exactly: 1.5 +
           2.5i gives 2.5, -3 + 4i gives 4, 0.25 - 0.5i gives -0.5.
test       t/001-finite.c

assertion  XSH.cimag.002
anchor     functions/cimag.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/cimag.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       cimag returns a zero imaginary part with its sign (for a type with
           negative zero), whatever the real part is.
test       t/002-signed-zero.c

assertion  XSH.cimag.003
anchor     functions/cimag.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/cimag.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       cimag returns an infinite or NaN imaginary part as it is, and the
           imaginary part when the real part is infinite or NaN.
test       t/003-infinite-nan.c
